# Run r1102b, worldgen slice, boot W1: group B fresh normal world "wge", seed 8675309 (compares with SQ-WG30).
# Setup: w_setup.md W1 (prep_srv.sh OUT_W1 wge B; srv toml [worldgen.earth_fill] log = "ALL",
# [worldgen.meta_structures] log = true). One boot for SQ-WGE-01 to -05, -06d (first half), -08, SQ-EFB-00 to -15,
# -17 to -22 (first world), SQ-PSW-00, -02 to -05. Cross-boot files go to $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w (census jsons,
# logs); captures (square centres) carry to W2 / W3 / W1b through RES/vars.json, so use ONE RES for all w_ batches.
# Squares are Chunky r 300 (r 400 for PL and HI, the WGE-03b squares), probed in 13x13-chunk tiles with /zq under
# (tools/scratch_query/qb_tiles.py) and judged offline with tools/scratch_query/efb_judge.py on logs/latest.log.
# /reload only in the last row (SQ-EFB-20): it drops Chunky commands. Resume with qrun.py --from ID.
pace 2

## SQ-EFB-00 | offline: worldgen tool tests (GroundMatch, EarthFill 113+, Meta print ALL)
shell bash $INST/tools/test_worldgen_tools.sh > ../twt.txt 2>&1; grep -nE "^==|ALL|FAIL|error:|Could not find" ../twt.txt | head -60; ! grep -qE "FAIL|error:|Could not find or load main class" ../twt.txt

## SQ-EFB-17 | offline: water reach and withBases checks in EarthFillTest
shell m=0; for p in "water reach 2" "no water reach" "water reach leaves air" "bury: water reach 2 too" "water reach above the beard" "no base tag" "sand base" "stone + sand"; do grep -F "$p" ../twt.txt || { echo "MISSING: $p"; m=1; }; done; [ $m = 0 ] && ! grep -qE "FAIL|error:" ../twt.txt

## SQ-PSW-00 | offline: worldgen json, nether scan, no glowstone line
shell (cd $INST && python3 tools/check_worldgen_json.py) > ../cwj.txt 2>&1; r1=$?; tail -8 ../cwj.txt; (cd $INST && python3 tools/nether_worldgen_scan.py) 2>&1 | tail -8; n=$(grep -c glowstone $INST/feature_writeup/nether_worldgen_scan.md || true); echo "check_worldgen_json rc $r1, glowstone lines $n"; [ "$r1" = 0 ] && [ "$n" = 0 ]
look check_worldgen_json: 0 problems; the scan prints 47 structures and a processor count

## SQ-WGE-08 | full-boot regression: ERROR count, mixin / exception lines, Done time, tick at 5 min
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (Mixin apply failed|InvalidInjectionException|Critical injection failure)
shell mkdir -p $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w; cp logs/latest.log $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w/w1_boot.log; grep -o "Done ([0-9.]*s)" logs/latest.log; echo "ERROR lines: $(grep -c ERROR logs/latest.log || true)"; grep -iE "mixin|exception" logs/latest.log | grep -v "Error loading class" | cut -c1-300 | head -40
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=wgehome] run summon minecraft:marker ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["wgehome"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=wgehome,limit=1] Pos
capture S entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
sleep 240
> forge tps
waitlog Overall 30
look ERROR count and the mixin / exception lines against the last clean group B boot (perf/runs/r1101 w2 or the SQ-WG30 boot); Done time within 10 % of SQ-WG30; Overall mean tick at about 5 min; the 9 World Generation changelog bullets each match a WGE row

## SQ-EFB-01 | probe: /zq under at spawn prints full lines; earth-fill log has lines (log = ALL)
bootexpect \[earth-fill\]
> zq under {S1} {S3} 4 -
waitlog \[zq\] (under: \d+ starts|error) 120
expect \[zq\] under: \d+ starts
reject \[zq\] error
reject Error occurred while handling event
shell echo "earth-fill lines: $(grep -c "\[earth-fill\]" logs/latest.log || true)"; grep "\[zq\] under " logs/latest.log | tail -5 | cut -c1-400
look the under lines carry every field (pieces, cols, air-below, water-below, base water, base earth, ring, foreign); 0 starts at an ocean spawn is a pass for the probe, rerun on a square tile (SQ-EFB-02) if so

## SQ-WGE-01a | End solver: shadowlands 0.75, no note for it, crystal peaks 3, void barrens 2
bootexpect \[biome-tuning\] override minecraft:the_end
bootreject \[biome-tuning\] note minecraft:the_end nullscape:shadowlands
bootreject (?i)(error|exception).*(BiomeLayoutTuner|biome-tuning)
shell grep -A1 '"nullscape:shadowlands"' kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_config.json | grep -q '"multiplier": 0.75' && grep -A1 '"nullscape:crystal_peaks"' kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_config.json | grep -q '"multiplier": 3' && grep -A1 '"nullscape:void_barrens"' kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_config.json | grep -q '"multiplier": 2'; r=$?; grep -a 'biome-tuning\]' logs/latest.log | sed 's/.*\[biome-tuning\]/[biome-tuning]/' | grep -iE 'the_end|nullscape' | cut -c1-300; exit $r
look the End line: shadowlands modelled share near 14 % (aim about 16 %); no solver note for it

