## SQ-PSW-02-y | Nether ruins: box y and biome
shell grep '\[zq\] under philipsruins:' logs/latest.log | cut -c1-260
look start boxes: city and dungeon bottoms near y 5 / y 12, rare ruin and blackstone ruin near y 33; biome (soul sand valley; crimson / warped; wastes / basalt deltas) and no lava flood: client tp to the captured NC / ND / NR / NS positions

## SQ-PSW-03 | meta/ruin_cluster found, anchored on a level-three ruin, towers or church
> locate structure creativeengineering:meta/ruin_cluster
waitlog (nearest creativeengineering:meta/ruin_cluster.* is at|type "?creativeengineering:meta/ruin_cluster|creativeengineering:meta/ruin_cluster.*timed out|Could not find) 200
expect nearest creativeengineering:meta/ruin_cluster.* is at

## SQ-PSW-03-b | meta/pillager_camp_ruin found, never on a rare ruin
> locate structure creativeengineering:meta/pillager_camp_ruin
waitlog (nearest creativeengineering:meta/pillager_camp_ruin.* is at|type "?creativeengineering:meta/pillager_camp_ruin|creativeengineering:meta/pillager_camp_ruin.*timed out|Could not find) 200
expect nearest creativeengineering:meta/pillager_camp_ruin.* is at
shell grep -aE 'meta-structures\].*(ruin_cluster|pillager_camp_ruin)' logs/latest.log | cut -c1-300 | tail -12
reject meta/(ruin_cluster|pillager_camp_ruin).*rare_ruin
look anchors named in the [meta-structures] lines (log = true): level-three ruin, ancient towers or forgotten church

## SQ-PSW-04 | no glowstone in the Overworld (spawn r 1000 + deep dark square)
> save-all flush
waitlog Saved the game 300
shell python3 -I $INST/tools/block_census.py wge minecraft:glowstone minecraft:soul_fire minecraft:soul_lantern > ../psw04.txt; head -30 ../psw04.txt; n=$(sed -n 's/^  minecraft:glowstone: \([0-9]*\) in.*/\1/p' ../psw04.txt); echo "glowstone $n"; [ "$n" = 0 ]
look a gothic church in the area shows yellow corundum (NW-11): client

## SQ-PSW-05 | End spires generate past 1050 blocks; bases on end stone
shell python3 -I $INST/tools/block_census.py wge quark:dusky_myalite quark:myalite_crystal --dim end > ../psw05.txt; head -12 ../psw05.txt; n=$(sed -n 's/^  quark:myalite_crystal: \([0-9]*\) in.*/\1/p' ../psw05.txt); [ "${n:-0}" -gt 0 ]
bootreject (?i)QuarkSpiralSpireFootprintMixin.*(fail|error)
look tp to 3 to 5 of the listed chunks and look under each spike from the side (client): end stone all round, none over the void

## SQ-WGE-01b-S | End biome sample (/dumpclimate 20,000 points): shadowlands 12 to 20 %, others within x1.3 of SQ-WG30-E03
> dumpclimate
waitlog (dumpclimate.* done in|\[dumpclimate\] .*failed) 1200
shell f=kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/climate/minecraft__the_end.json.gz; mkdir -p $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w; cp $f $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w/w1_end_climate.json.gz; python3 -I $INST/tools/scratch_query/climate_share.py $f --min nullscape:shadowlands 12 20 --min nullscape:crystal_peaks 4.06 6.86 --min nullscape:void_barrens 5.47 9.24; r=$?; cp $INST/kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/climate/*.json.gz kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/climate/; echo restored the instance samples; exit $r
# the restore keeps the next world load / reload on the shipped samples (BiomeLayoutTuner reads a new dump)

## SQ-EFB-20 | sand_base tag lists the 8 sandstones, terracottas, 3 Philip blocks; no unresolved key; /reload clean (LAST: drops Chunky)
kjsreject (?i)(philips_sand_stone_brick|philips_red_sand_stone_brick|philips_sandstone_tiles).*(unknown|unresolved|missing|not found)
bootreject (?i)(philips_sand_stone_brick|philips_red_sand_stone_brick|philips_sandstone_tiles).*(unknown|unresolved|missing|not found)
> zq blocktag creativeengineering:earth_fill/sand_base
waitlog \[zq\] done 60
expect blocktag creativeengineering:earth_fill/sand_base \(\d+\): .*philips
expect blocktag creativeengineering:earth_fill/sand_base \(\d+\): .*terracotta
shell mkdir -p $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w; cp logs/latest.log $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w/w1_latest.log; pwd > $INST/perf/runs/r1103w/w/w1_srv_path; echo saved W1 log and path
> reload
sleep 40
reject \[earth-fill\] blocks:.*(holds no block|unknown)
look the tag line: 8 forge:sandstone blocks, the terracottas, the 3 Philip blocks
